WEBVTT

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:49.470
So Gavan and his men captured
the Earthnoids then, huh?

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:50.810
Yeah.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:55.810
The Amerians who went to Wharf #4 got into
a machine battle with Gavan and his men.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:59.150
It seems the Dorette Army have
their hands full dealing with them.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.780
Which means we can breathe easy for now.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.440
That's one big bulkhead.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:06.950
Are those people part of your group too?

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.570
- ﻿Nope.
- Wow!

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.290
﻿- Did these come from Mars or Venus?
- They're olive trees.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:20.170
You have a good number that
have to be 500 years old here.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:24.670
Compared to the land we saw
earlier, these fields are...

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:30.010
The cultivation of hemp and sesame
has been permitted recently.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:33.850
- Why is that?
- ﻿Because this was Rayhunton family land.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.850
Rayhunton? Rayhunton land?

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.860
Why is this place lower than the rest?

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.450
This used to be underground.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:52.280
But then it caved in...
You can enter this way.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.870
Do you think maybe it's
space right beneath us?

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.290
Looks like.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.290
- Lorucca, I've brought them.
- ﻿It was operator error.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.630
So I'll have the paperwork
delivered to you tomorrow.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:06.420
- Is that acceptable?
- ﻿Please, have a seat.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.880
Right.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.470
I've really put you through a lot

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.470
It must have been hard.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.890
It's good of you to come all this way.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:22.610
- I am Miraji Barbaros.
- ﻿Donyell Toss.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.360
Please, take a seat...
Or perhaps you should get changed first?

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.450
Yeah, let's do that.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:34.370
Please do, Princess! Prince!

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:49.510
So, we just want to stop the
Dorette Fleets Operation Reconguista.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:54.720
The question is, why are they carrying
out their plan to return to Earth now?

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.220
It's General Noutu Dorette being hasty.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:01.020
Do you suppose there's no way
to make them call it off?

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.480
That's...

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:04.690
My princess...

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.650
You look just like your mother...
P-Pardon me.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.070
There are problems here in Towasanga as well,

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:18.910
but the cause is the birth of a generation
on Earth that views war as fun and games.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.500
Are you talking about my generation?

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.120
Oh, no, my prince, it's not like that...

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:26.750
I engaged in space piracy
using the G-Self as well.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.960
We share some of the responsibility for that.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:36.550
We had the unit we constructed adopted as
an advance scout for the Dorette Fleet.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:40.270
The G-Self's saved our lives over and over.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.980
We call it the YG-111.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.230
Just before it departed for Earth,

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:49.980
we installed a function in it that
we hadn't informed Raraiya of.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:56.030
So, we caused both of you
undue trouble as a result.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:01.790
I would like to show you
the place of your birth.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.670
As the Rayhunton princess...

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.540
And the Rayhunton prince.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.170
Huh?

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.960
What did you just say?

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:12.470
It's got to be some sort of joke.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:13.930
Or not.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.180
Heave-ho!

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:24.100
- Okay, there it goes.
- It's coming down!

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:29.020
- That's good!
- Do that a bit quieter!

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.690
You'll bother the neighbors!

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.070
This is the nursery.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.370
- Do you remember it?
- ﻿No clue.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:42.370
I don't remember this at all.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.710
Hey, do you think I might have used that?

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:48.630
It was a mystery to me how
you fell out of it so often.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:51.340
- Yeah! Like that!
- ﻿We can pull this one down too!

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:53.670
Be careful this time!

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.680
Oh, this atmosphere...

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.720
Suddenly, I do feel that I know this place.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.560
What could it be?

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:16.700
Here. It was here!

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:24.410
What I wanted to remember, but never could.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.960
I had wondered for the
longest time what it was.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:30.420
What I wanted to recall.

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:40.180
Miss Aida.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:43.720
I've only ever known my mom and dad.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:47.640
My mother said she'd thrown out my
father's pictures and all data on him.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:50.940
There is a picture from
around the same time here.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.610
These are your parents.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:02.280
The image which he is holding
is the only one we have.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:06.200
The rest of their data was
deleted by the Dorette family.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:07.710
Ah... Those are...

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.830
They were in a drawer
on top of the bookshelf.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:21.010
On the orders of Captain Piani Kaluta,
you were sent to take refuge on Earth.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.180
So you were treated as orphans.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:27.730
We thought it would be safest
for you to remain unaware of it,

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.140
but we wanted to find you,

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:32.560
so we installed a device in the G-Self.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:35.360
Oh! You mean the Rayhunton Codes, right?

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.700
Ah! The first time I touched the G-Self...

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:41.410
You should have one of these too, Miss Aida.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:45.120
That's...! I have the same thing.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:50.000
The touch sensors can pick up
your DNA from sweat and blood.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.870
It used retinal and
fingerprint scans as well

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.630
to allow direct descendants of the
Rayhunton family to control it.

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:04.470
Because of this system of yours,

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.890
we have been forced to confront
incredibly harsh realities.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.730
Of course, part of this is the
dispositions we inherited

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:15.730
from the Zenam and
Surugan families who raised us.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:18.940
However, because we could control the G-Self,

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:21.030
my lover was killed,

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:25.620
and Bellri was... My brother was forced
to bear the disgrace of becoming a killer.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:30.870
You may have a duty...

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:33.370
An ideal you strive for, but still...

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:37.670
I will find such things for
myself, and accomplish them.

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:39.170
Sis...

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:43.050
New eras are not created by old people.

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:54.600
I figured.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:58.360
What's so funny?

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:02.990
That our genius buddy Captain Klim was
angry he couldn't pilot the G-Self.

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:07.950
He even dragged Raraiya out for it...
What's wrong?

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:09.990
What will we do from here on?

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.960
Flaminia and her people's information
should be useful to us.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:17.420
The Dorette Fleet wants to make allies
of the Megafauna and Salamandra.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:18.210
Right.

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:20.380
- So...
- ﻿We're leaving now.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.590
My princess, may I have a word?

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:24.340
Sorry to have worried you.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.360
Even a single piece of toilet paper
is a precious commodity here!

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.530
What do you think you're
doing, releasing a container?

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:44.950
Deck Chief, have them
put their backs into it!

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.820
Turn the magnets in your boots
on and dig your heels in!

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.620
- Captain.
- ﻿Yeah?

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:56.290
The light to the north of the solar panels
is a mineral extraction facility, right?

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.790
That's right. It's a fairly large scale one.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.840
That's the equatorial belt, right?

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.800
Don't you think we're being tricked?

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:10.760
It has a history of over 2000 years,
including the Universal Century.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.810
Soon, Towasanga's Cyrano-5
will come into view.

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:17.230
Was it built using an asteroid as its core?

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:20.610
Yes, but it's not what you're imagining.

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:26.070
What is that? It looks like a lantern.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:30.910
They say the central meteor looks
like Cyrano de Bergerac's nose.

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:32.620
- ﻿I see.
- ﻿Well...

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:41.840
Well, it must be a nation with the industrial
capacity to send out the Dorette Fleet.

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:44.460
We've entered Towasanga territory.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:47.510
All mobile suits take up alert positions.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:49.550
Even if we negotiate for
permission to enter port,

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.810
we mustn't let our guards down
until we're actually in port.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:54.100
Well, of course.

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:58.190
What is it?

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:01.690
Do you trust Colonel Cumpa?

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:03.690
It's precisely because I trust him

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:08.910
that I could come here, leaving the
Dorette Fleet surrounding Capital Tower.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:09.950
Captain!

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:13.660
I've heard this ship will be surrendering
to the Towasangan forces.

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:14.790
Don't use radio!

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:18.710
- We're already in Towasanga's territory.
- ﻿Right.

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:21.500
If we want to take their
military power back with us,

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.290
we need to become their allies temporarily.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:26.010
- Temporarily?
- Now you get it.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:29.130
- That's the plan?
- ﻿Exactly.

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:32.680
Manny Ambassada, take the utmost caution.

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:35.600
Y-Yes, Captain!

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.680
That's my Luin!

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:44.270
Hmph, Mask is soft on that woman, is he?

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:32.950
They're entering Cyrano-5's
Apache Military Port?

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:33.990
The Capital Army's warship
the Garanden, right?

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:36.080
This is the greatest happening
since the founding of Towasanga.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:37.750
They want to take that thing into port
in the heart of the Dorette Fleet?

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:40.750
A ship constructed by Earthnoids will
be entering Apache Military Port!

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.250
The sender is a man named
Colonel Cumpa Rusita.

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:44.590
Of the four ships which came earlier, the
Salamandra is also at Apache Military Port, but...

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:45.710
Are you familiar with him?

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:47.130
Of course not.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:49.630
Is it really the Garanden?

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:51.930
Then the Mask Corps are here too!

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.550
That's an incident waiting to happen!

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:56.220
An incident! An incident!

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:16.490
What? Are the guys from the fleet
going out to greet the Earthnoid ship?

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:20.960
We don't know what those Earthnoid
Mobile Suits might do.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:25.540
What do you think you're doing to my Hecate?

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:27.500
Bear with it, Mick.

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:35.180
Do we not need to head out as well?

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:39.850
This is the Gavan Team's territory.
Our job right now is to welcome them.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.730
Won't the Amerian Army beat us to the punch?

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:43.810
Why do you think that?

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:48.070
Ameria's Salamandra is being treated
as an honored guest by military HQ.

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:51.700
They'll be enemies of the Capital Army
ship that's about to make port here.

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:53.200
- Listen...
- ﻿Huh?

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:57.910
If we let them into port here,
then both of them are ours.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.040
Why can't you understand these things?

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.870
Did you see the guys who went out there?

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.670
Aren't you worried they'll sink the Garanden?

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:10.210
It was likely Colonel Cumpa Rusita of the
Research Departments idea to come here.

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:11.420
So that will not happen.

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:16.100
If the Capital Army has come here to
forge an alliance with the Dorette Fleet,

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:18.010
what will happen to our alliance?

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:20.220
We can all be good friends!

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:25.520
Captain! The moment they found
out you're the president's son,

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:28.440
they started treating us like
VIPs and gave us supplies.

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:31.990
The Hazm Government and the military
have their own circumstances.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:37.490
I bet you're planning to seize control of
the Dorette Fleet before the Capital Army does.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:42.250
Then, when we get back to Earth, you
want to take control of the government.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.500
Say no more.

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:49.460
Bellri, don't just arbitrarily
decide to go out there!

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.550
So you <i>were</i> planning on going out alone.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.510
If even the Garanden has come here,

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:56.510
we need to go there directly and
ask what's up, don't you think?

00:14:56.510 --> 00:14:59.140
You're going there to ask
what the situation is?

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:01.770
Bellri! Why you...

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:04.600
Bellri! We can't move recklessly right now!

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:10.230
Adam, why didn't you stop him?

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:13.280
- I never thought he'd actually go out.
- Happa!

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.580
Up there, or rather...

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:30.500
<i>﻿On top of this thing there are forests,</i>

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.420
<i>﻿farms built on caved in land,</i>

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:35.130
<i>﻿even the house where I was born and ponds?</i>

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:39.850
<i>﻿I-It's hard to think my homeland is
a place that looks like this...</i>

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:44.560
<i>﻿Even if this thing had my
parents' DNA loaded into it...</i>

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:47.230
<i>﻿When I'm already straining
to accept all this...</i>

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.520
Why did the Garanden have to come here?

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:53.110
Wasn't Mask's mission
to beat the Dorette Fleet?

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.780
G-Self, this is a homecoming for
you too, so bring me up a map!

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:05.200
Where's the Apache Military Port? Here?

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:06.870
That's the Garanden?!

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:12.630
I see. If it's a ship under the
direct command of Colonel Cumpa,

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:14.340
maybe it's not that strange
for it to have come here.

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:16.800
Not strange?

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:19.010
Actually, it's not strange.
It's downright weird!

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:28.100
The Mobile Suit that came from
Ring #5 South is the YG-111, isn't it?

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:31.690
That suit was sent out for recon
as part of Operation Reconguista.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:33.610
It's Raraiya Akuparl's.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:34.860
Yeah.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:37.400
1st and 2nd squads, follow me.

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:40.660
3rd squad, watch the
Garanden and guide them in!

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:41.240
Yes sir!

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:52.460
Why did you send Bell out alone?

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:54.670
No one gave him permission to go out.

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:56.840
Lieutenant, please go drag Bellri back here.

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:58.720
That's the plan.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:01.970
But why is Towasanga welcoming the Garanden?

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.850
They hate them!

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:06.810
The guys who were left behind
hate the ones in the fleet.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.980
- Right?
- They do?

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:12.060
There's lots of guys who'd
like to live on Earth,

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:15.690
so they hate people like Raraiya
who got to go down there.

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:17.730
We have to protect her!

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:20.400
And he goes and lays his hands
all over her while he says it.

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:21.820
Huh? Miss Aida.

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:26.540
I'm borrowing the Moran!

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:28.950
This area is defended by the Gavan Team!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:30.450
That's why I'm going out!

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:31.920
You're crazy!

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:33.670
Raraiya?

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:35.630
Raraiya Akuparl!

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:37.920
What are you doing returning without notice?

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:40.630
"Returning without notice?" What?

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:47.180
Judging from your lack of response,

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.640
it's an Earthnoid piloting that machine!

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:51.600
What?!

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:53.980
<i>﻿He's calling me an Earthnoid
even though I was born here?</i>

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:01.030
Get away from the ring!

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:03.160
I can't blow you up like this!

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:06.450
S-So what!

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:13.500
Are you going to resist?!

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.380
You don!t know anything about me!

00:18:28.430 --> 00:18:29.810
I-Is this...

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:31.560
the YG...?!

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.270
I won't kill you.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:35.520
But if you get in our way ever again,

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:37.270
there will be no such mercy!

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:39.860
I have a sister, you know,
so next time I'll do it!

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:42.150
Th-That form...

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:45.360
Long ago, there was one...
c-called Gundam or something...

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:46.570
We're returning to base!

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.080
Bell! Bellri!

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:51.450
Are you okay?

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:52.870
We heard everything.

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:54.920
I was watching on the long-range monitor.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:57.130
You shut that Zacks up in no time.

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.630
I'm happy for you as a former
instructor, but how did you do it?

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:04.590
B-But I just scratched it up.

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:06.300
Nothing could have happened to the pilot.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:07.840
I didn't do anything like that!

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:09.970
W-We understand that.

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:11.560
You did well.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:13.230
- This is bad.
- ﻿Huh?

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:16.850
You can't show the armies of
Towasanga this kind of firepower!

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:19.360
So don't move the G-Self any more.

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:21.480
- Bellri!
- ﻿Y-Yes sir!

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:23.440
Let me do that.

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:30.240
Bellri, you're okay, right?

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.490
Bellri!

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.410
I'm fine.

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:41.130
<i>﻿You want me to call this thing my home land?</i>

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:55.140
What are you so happy about?

00:19:55.140 --> 00:20:01.190
Well, they actually let the Garanden
into the Apache Military Port here!

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:03.900
This may be where the
mastermind shows himself.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:07.240
There's no way the Earthnoids
could build this on their own.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:10.490
They say a lot of engineers have illegally
immigrated from here to Earth.

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:13.410
- Prime Minister Hazm is here to greet them?
- ﻿I hear Commander Zurchin is coming too.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:15.370
- ﻿I can't see why the Earthnoids would come.
- Probably to win the war on Earth.

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:18.290
- Will Towasanga help the Capital Tower?
- Will we have freedom of movement after this?

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:20.420
It's good of you to come all this way.

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:23.750
For the kind treatment the Hazm Government
and the military have afforded us,

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:25.130
you have my heartfelt thanks.

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:28.760
This is the time of year when the
Kashiba Mikoshi descends,

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:31.010
- so we aren't sufficiently prepared to—
- ﻿Prime Minister.

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:33.760
- You are before guests.
- Oh, yes.

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:37.640
If anything does not meet your satisfaction,
please, tell the person in charge.

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:42.310
What became of the ship which
came before ours, the Megafauna?

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:44.150
They're waiting to dock.

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:46.570
Because the Salamandra is coming in now.

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:49.990
Mr. Happa, you can use our parts as well.

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:51.990
Look how this broke!

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:54.200
What we need is more hands!

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:56.830
We'll have some of our experts help.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:59.000
I'm an expert on this as well.

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:00.750
That will help.

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:03.170
Can we go up to the pilots' rooms from here?

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:05.130
It's the elevator over there.

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:09.840
What's wrong with me thinking
I did better than Genius Klim?

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:12.140
You have surpassed the captain.

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:14.180
Thanks to the G-Self's superior specs.

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:18.180
But without someone who can use it
properly, those high specs mean nothing.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:20.190
Well, yes...

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:23.440
But was that battle necessary?

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:25.900
I nearly got electrocuted.

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:27.360
By that weird trap!

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:29.650
- May we come in?
- ﻿Oh, sure.

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:32.410
It's all these people's fault
that things ended up like this!

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:33.780
Prince Bellri!

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:37.700
Besides, the Megafauna is being monitored
by the Dorette Fleet, isn't it?

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:41.210
Your anti-war movement
is never going to work!

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:45.420
At present, with preparations for both
the descent of the Kashiba Mikoshi

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:49.800
and the return of the Crescent Ship to the
Venus Globe, Towasanga is in disorder.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:52.590
My prince! Do you mean to fight again?

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:55.970
In space, we need to focus just on surviving.

00:21:55.970 --> 00:21:58.470
That is the ironclad rule
of the Capital Guard.

00:21:58.470 --> 00:22:01.310
If you didn't just arbitrarily decide
you were going to the Garanden...

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:04.310
If they tell me Aida's my sister,

00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:07.070
yeah, that's gonna drive me a little crazy!

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:10.780
Clen Moa, I want you to
swap out the Chip Box.

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:14.320
The deck crew is helping out
with the backpack's coating.

00:22:14.320 --> 00:22:16.910
We're gonna be working all night tonight.
All night, you got that?

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:19.660
Rayhunton nothing!

00:22:19.660 --> 00:22:22.790
Bring me the XPP Box.

00:22:22.790 --> 00:22:25.040
Even Jama's doing it.

00:24:00.850 --> 00:24:04.010
Raraiya ends up using the Neodu
which she learns to pilot.

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:07.850
Because the Mask Corps was having
Barara use a new machine as well,

00:24:07.850 --> 00:24:09.270
they got into a fight.

00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:13.480
But, after that, friend and
foe alike went out

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:17.490
to be space trash collectors
on the far side of the moon.

00:24:18.320 --> 00:24:22.120
Next time on Reconguista in G,
"﻿Aida's Decision."

00:24:22.120 --> 00:24:25.620
If you want to understand the
story, you'll have to watch.
